image/fetch/$s_!Z89d!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe885be51-755c-4971-805e-26078774899f_4284x5712.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Z89d!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fe885be51-755c-4971-805e-26078774899f_4284x5712.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Playfully posing in my attractive Acacia Clinics fleece in London.</figcaption></figure></div><p>I was recently interviewed for the Carlat Psychiatry Podcast about some of these articles, and some of that tape appears in the two-part series they did on what went wrong in the MAPS/Lykos trials, as reviewed by an FDA Advisory Committee recently.</p><p>Part 1:</p><div class=\"apple-podcast-container\" data-component-name=\"ApplePodcastToDom\"><iframe class=\"apple-podcast \" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000658416842&quot;,&quot;isEpisode&quot;:true,&quot;imageUrl&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/podcast-episode_1000658416842.jpg&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;MDMA: What Went Wrong Part 1&quot;,&quot;podcastTitle&quot;:&quot;The Carlat Psychiatry Podcast&quot;,&quot;podcastByline&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:1201000,&quot;numEpisodes&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;targetUrl&quot;:&quot;https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/mdma-what-went-wrong-part-1/id1463414537?i=1000658416842&amp;uo=4&quot;,&quot;releaseDate&quot;:&quot;2024-06-10T06:00:00Z&quot;}\" src=\"https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000658416842\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay *; encrypted-media *;\" allowfullscreen=\"true\"></iframe></div><p></p><p>Part 2:</p><div class=\"apple-podcast-container\" data-component-name=\"ApplePodcastToDom\"><iframe class=\"apple-podcast \" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000659233975&quot;,&quot;isEpisode&quot;:true,&quot;imageUrl&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/podcast-episode_1000659233975.jpg&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;MDMA: What Went Wrong Part 2&quot;,&quot;podcastTitle&quot;:&quot;The Carlat Psychiatry Podcast&quot;,&quot;podcastByline&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;numEpisodes&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;targetUrl&quot;:&quot;https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/mdma-what-went-wrong-part-2/id1463414537?i=1000659233975&amp;uo=4&quot;,&quot;releaseDate&quot;:&quot;2024-06-17T06:00:00Z&quot;}\" src=\"https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000659233975\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay *; encrypted-media *;\" allowfullscreen=\"true\"></iframe></div><p>This is not the last word on MDMA-AT, MDMA, or any other psychedelic medicine.   It is a reminder that extraordinary claims require extraordinary evidence.   We have been here before in the medical discipline of psychiatry.  <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/clozapine-part-i?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Clozapine was a radically different medicine</a> that was both killing people with rare but deadly side effects <em>and</em> appeared more effective than prior treatments.   </p><p>In the case of clozapine, the FDA required a high bar for approval—it had to be monitored for safety, it needed to be better than existing treatments, and it needed to work in treatment-resistant patients.  </p><p>I reviewed <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/clozapine-part-i?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">some of that history in a prior article.</a></p><p>Thanks for reading, listening, and joining the future of psychiatry as we, in a very clumsy manner, try to <em>get to the future</em> without the house of medicine burning down in the process.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/what-went-wrong-mdma-on-the-carlat?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/what-went-wrong-mdma-on-the-carlat?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p>I’ll remind readers they can access my prior writing on the topic here—but some of it is behind a paywall.  PAY TO SUBSCRIBE.  It encourages me :)</p><h5>Prequels.</h5><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/mdma-now-everyone-is-interested-in?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Now, Everyone Is Interested in Drug Development</a></p><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/how-big-of-a-deal-are-psychedelic?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">How Big of a Deal are Psychedelic Medicines Likely to Be?</a></p><h3>The “Saving MDMA” Series!</h3><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/can-mdma-at-be-saved-part-i?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Can MDMA-AT Be Saved, Part I</a></p><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/can-mdma-at-be-saved-part-ii?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Can MDMA-AT Be Saved, Part II</a></p><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/should-mdma-at-be-saved-part-iii?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Should MDMA-AT Be Saved, Part III</a></p><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/saving-mdma-from-at-part-iv?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Saving MDMA from AT: Part IV</a></p><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/bad-touch-saving-mdma-part-v?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Bad Touch!: MDMA Part V</a></p><p><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/saving-mdma-and-other-psychedelic?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=true\">Saving MDMA (and other psychedelic therapies), Part VI</a></p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">The Frontier Psychiatrists  is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><p></p><p></p>","text":"The Frontier Psychiatrists is a daily-enough health-themed newsletter…that tries to have a laugh while exploring serious topics.\n\nEvery once in a while, Owen Muir, M.D., also gets to crank out serious academic work. Much of that has been on topics of neuromodulation, Ai diagnostics, and psychedelic medicine. For new readers, there is a bar at the top of the website version that lets you visit my Google Scholar publications. Or just click here.\n\nPlayfully posing in my attractive Acacia Clinics fleece in London.\n\nI was recently interviewed for the Carlat Psychiatry Podcast about some of these articles, and some of that tape appears in the two-part series they did on what went wrong in the MAPS/Lykos trials, as reviewed by an FDA Advisory Committee recently.\n\nPart 1:\n\nPart 2:\n\nThis is not the last word on MDMA-AT, MDMA, or any other psychedelic medicine. It is a reminder that extraordinary claims require extraordinary evidence. We have been here before in the medical discipline of psychiatry. Clozapine was a radically different medicine that was both killing people with rare but deadly side effects and appeared more effective than prior treatments.\n\nIn the case of clozapine, the FDA required a high bar for approval—it had to be monitored for safety, it needed to be better than existing treatments, and it needed to work in treatment-resistant patients.\n\nI reviewed some of that history in a prior article.\n\nThanks for reading, listening, and joining the future of psychiatry as we, in a very clumsy manner, try to get to the future without the house of medicine burning down in the process.\n\nShare\n\nSubscribe now\n\nI’ll remind readers they can access my prior writing on the topic here—but some of it is behind a paywall. PAY TO SUBSCRIBE. It encourages me :)\n\nPrequels.\n\nNow, Everyone Is Interested in Drug Development\n\nHow Big of a Deal are Psychedelic Medicines Likely to Be?\n\nThe “Saving MDMA” Series!\n\nCan MDMA-AT Be Saved, Part I\n\nCan MDMA-AT Be Saved, Part II\n\nShould MDMA-AT Be Saved, Part III\n\nSaving MDMA from AT: Part IV\n\nBad Touch!: MDMA Part V\n\nSaving MDMA (and other psychedelic therapies), Part VI\n\nThe Frontier Psychiatrists is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber."}